<div id="pfad" class="pf w0 h0" data-page-no="ad"><div class="pc pcad w0 h0"><img class="bi x0 y0 w1 h1" alt="" src="data:image/png;base64,"/><div class="c x1 y65 w2 hb"><div class="t m0 x6 h5 y1e3 ff17 fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">day overnight during of<span class="_ _1"></span>f-hours to provide daily reporting, but other</div><div class="t m0 x6 h5 yb2d ff17 fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">frequencies can also be used.</div><div class="t m0 x6 h5 yec9 ff17 fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">Size-based batch ingestion (<span class="fc2">Figure 4-10</span>) is quite common when data is</div><div class="t m0 x6 h5 yb2f ff17 fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">moved from a streaming-based system into object storage—ultimately<span class="_ _2"></span>, the</div><div class="t m0 x6 h5 yb30 ff17 fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">data must be cut into discrete blocks for future processing in a data lake.</div><div class="t m0 x6 h5 yb31 ff17 fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">Size-based ingestion systems such as Kinesis Firehose can break data into</div><div class="t m0 x6 h5 yb32 ff17 fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">objects based on a variety of criteria, such as size bytes of the total number</div><div class="t m0 x6 h5 yb33 ff17 fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">of events.</div></div><a class="l" href="#pfae" data-dest-detail='[174,"XYZ",76.5,720,null]'><div class="d m1" style="border-style:none;position:absolute;left:401.960833px;bottom:1074.754902px;width:69.750000px;height:16.500000px;background-color:rgba(255,255,255,0.000001);"></div></a></div><div class="pi" data-data='{"ctm":[1.633987,0.000000,0.000000,1.633987,0.000000,0.000000]}'></div></div>
